-- ccc10-sexual-services.l4 -- sections 286.1 to 286.5 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46: commodification of sexual activity
-- (obtaining sexual services, material benefit, procuring, advertising, and the immunities). Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE (every element holds, or the immunity applies); JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words, quoted in the branch's comment);
-- NOTHING (not covered: an element is missing, the text is silent or limits a prohibition in its own wording, or the answer points outside the text).
-- A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Seams: `s 197(1) ...` is ccc8's answer (the keel's PLAN.md names it as one input; here two); `s 787(1) ...` is ccc29's.
-- Dollar amounts are the text's own; no figure comes from memory.

§ `s 286.1 -- Obtaining sexual services for consideration`

-- 286.1(5): "place" and "public place" mean what subsection 197(1) says; the answers are s 197(1)'s (ccc8) and are passed through unchanged.
-- src:5806 | Definitions of place and public place
-- src:5807 | (5) For the purposes of this section, place and public place have the same meaning as in subsection 197(1).
@ref s 286.1(5) (src:5806-5807)
GIVEN `s 197(1) the place is a place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.1(5) the place is a place, as in subsection 197(1)` MEANS `s 197(1) the place is a place`

@ref s 286.1(5) (src:5806-5807)
GIVEN `s 197(1) the place is a public place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.1(5) the place is a public place, as in subsection 197(1)` MEANS `s 197(1) the place is a public place`

-- 286.1(1): the offence "in any place".
-- src:5780 | Obtaining sexual services for consideration
-- src:5781 | 286.1 (1) Everyone who, in any place, obtains for consideration, or communicates with anyone for the purpose of obtaining for consideration, the sexual services of a person is guilty of
@ref s 286.1(1) lead-in (src:5780-5781)
GIVEN `s 197(1) the place is a place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person obtains for consideration, or communicates with anyone for the purpose of obtaining for consideration, the sexual services of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.1(1) the person is guilty of the offence of obtaining sexual services for consideration` MEANS
    IF `the person obtains for consideration, or communicates with anyone for the purpose of obtaining for consideration, the sexual services of a person` AND (`s 197(1) the place is a place` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who, in any place, obtains for consideration, or communicates with anyone for the purpose of obtaining for consideration, the sexual services of a person" (the place is s 197(1)'s, which may be not determined)

@ref s 286.1(1) (src:5780-5781)
`s 286.1(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

-- 286.1(1)(a)(i) and (b)(i): the kind of place that raises the minimum fine. "in a public place, or in any place open to public view, that is or is next to a park ...".
-- src:5783 | (i) in the case where the offence is committed in a public place, or in any place open to public view, that is or is next to a park or the grounds of a school or religious institution or that is or is next to any other place where persons under the age of 18 can reasonably be expected to be present,
@ref s 286.1(1)(a)(i) (src:5783)
GIVEN `s 197(1) the place is a public place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the place is open to public view` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the place is, or is next to, a park or the grounds of a school or religious institution, or is, or is next to, any other place where persons under the age of 18 can reasonably be expected to be present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.1(1)(a)(i) the offence is committed in a place of the kind described` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF ((`s 197(1) the place is a public place` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR `the place is open to public view`) AND `the place is, or is next to, a park or the grounds of a school or religious institution, or is, or is next to, any other place where persons under the age of 18 can reasonably be expected to be present` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (`s 197(1) the place is a public place` EQUALS NOTHING) AND (NOT `the place is open to public view`) AND `the place is, or is next to, a park or the grounds of a school or religious institution, or is, or is next to, any other place where persons under the age of 18 can reasonably be expected to be present` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the place is a public place is s 197(1)'s and is not determined
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in any other case" (the other limb of the paragraph, sub-paragraph (ii), is the complement of sub-paragraph (i))

-- 286.1(1): the punishment. A ladder of eight cells: mode (indictment, summary), the kind of place, first or subsequent offence.
-- src:5782 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years and a minimum punishment of,
-- src:5783 | (i) in the case where the offence is committed in a public place, or in any place open to public view, that is or is next to a park or the grounds of a school or religious institution or that is or is next to any other place where persons under the age of 18 can reasonably be expected to be present,
-- src:5784 | (A) for a first offence, a fine of $2,000, and
-- src:5785 | (B) for each subsequent offence, a fine of $4,000, or
-- src:5786 | (ii) in any other case,
-- src:5787 | (A) for a first offence, a fine of $1,000, and
-- src:5788 | (B) for each subsequent offence, a fine of $2,000; or
-- src:5789 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction and liable to a fine of not more than $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term of not more than two years less a day, or to both, and to a minimum punishment of,
-- src:5790 | (i) in the case referred to in subparagraph (a)(i),
-- src:5791 | (A) for a first offence, a fine of $1,000, and
-- src:5792 | (B) for each subsequent offence, a fine of $2,000, or
-- src:5793 | (ii) in any other case,
-- src:5794 | (A) for a first offence, a fine of $500, and
-- src:5795 | (B) for each subsequent offence, a fine of $1,000.
@ref s 286.1(1)(a) and (b) (src:5782-5795)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `the answer of s 286.1(1)(a)(i)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 286.1(1) as to a subsequent offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 286.1(1) the punishment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 286.1(1)(a)(i)` EQUALS NOTHING) OR (`the answer of s 286.1(1) as to a subsequent offence` EQUALS NOTHING)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the kind of place (s 197(1)) or whether the offence is a subsequent one (s 286.1(1) and (4)) is not determined
        IF mode EQUALS `by indictment`
        THEN JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, (`a fine of` (`the minimum fine on indictment`)))
        OTHERWISE JUST (Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years less a day`), `no imprisonment is stated`, (`a fine of` 5000), (`a fine of` (`the minimum fine on summary conviction`)))
    WHERE
        `the kind of place applies` MEANS `the answer of s 286.1(1)(a)(i)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        `the offence is a subsequent one` MEANS `the answer of s 286.1(1) as to a subsequent offence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        -- ruler: the minimum fine in dollars. Indictment: (a)(i)(A) 2,000 and (B) 4,000; (a)(ii)(A) 1,000 and (B) 2,000. Summary: (b)(i)(A) 1,000 and (B) 2,000; (b)(ii)(A) 500 and (B) 1,000.
        `the minimum fine on indictment` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of place applies` AND `the offence is a subsequent one` THEN 4000
                IF `the kind of place applies` THEN 2000
                IF `the offence is a subsequent one` THEN 2000
                OTHERWISE 1000
        `the minimum fine on summary conviction` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the kind of place applies` AND `the offence is a subsequent one` THEN 2000
                IF `the kind of place applies` THEN 1000
                IF `the offence is a subsequent one` THEN 1000
                OTHERWISE 500

-- 286.1(3) and (4): which earlier convictions count, and how the sequence is read. The text states the list "for the purpose of subsection (2)" and states
-- (4) "for the purposes of this section": for subsection (1) only (4) applies, and an earlier conviction counts if it is of an offence under subsection (1) (fork F35).
-- src:5800 | Subsequent offences
-- src:5801 | (3) In determining, for the purpose of subsection (2), whether a convicted person has committed a subsequent offence, if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence:
-- src:5802 | (a) an offence under that subsection; or
-- src:5803 | (b) an offence under subsection 212(4) of this Act, as it read from time to time before the day on which this subsection comes into force.
@ref s 286.1(3) (src:5800-5803)
DECLARE `s 286.1(3) earlier conviction` HAS
    `the offence of which the person was convicted`                                  IS A `Provision of the Code`
    `the offence was under subsection 212(4) of this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which subsection 286.1(3) comes into force`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`                      IS A DATE

@ref s 286.1(3) (src:5800-5803)
GIVEN conviction IS A `s 286.1(3) earlier conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.1(3) the conviction is of an offence to be considered as an earlier offence` MEANS
    IF (conviction's `the offence of which the person was convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 286.1 AND conviction's `the offence of which the person was convicted`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)")
       OR conviction's `the offence was under subsection 212(4) of this Act as it read from time to time before the day on which subsection 286.1(3) comes into force`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the person was earlier convicted of any of the following offences, that offence is to be considered as an earlier offence" (the list is not closed by "only")

-- src:5804 | Sequence of convictions only
-- src:5805 | (4) In determining, for the purposes of this section, whether a convicted person has committed a subsequent offence, the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions and no consideration shall be given to the sequence of commission of offences, whether any offence occurred before or after any conviction or whether offences were prosecuted by indictment or by way of summary conviction proceedings.
@ref s 286.1(4) (src:5804-5805)
GIVEN `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.1(4) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence`) LESS THAN (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the earlier offence`) GREATER THAN (DATE_SERIAL `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions" (a conviction that follows in the sequence is not an earlier one; whether the offences were prosecuted by indictment or summarily is not considered)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text does not say how two convictions on the same day are sequenced

@ref s 286.1(4) (src:5804-5805)
GIVEN `the earlier convictions` IS A LIST OF `s 286.1(3) earlier conviction`
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.1(2) the person has committed a subsequent offence` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN c IS A `s 286.1(3) earlier conviction` YIELD (`the conviction counts` c) EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the earlier convictions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN c IS A `s 286.1(3) earlier conviction` YIELD (`the conviction counts` c) EQUALS NOTHING) `the earlier convictions`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): an earlier conviction of an offence the subsection does not list, or on the same day, is not said to count or not to count
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a first offence" (no earlier conviction counts: none, or each follows the present one in the sequence)
    WHERE
        `the conviction counts` c MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF (`s 286.1(4) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` (c's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`) `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions"
                IF (`s 286.1(4) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` (c's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`) `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two convictions on one day
                OTHERWISE `s 286.1(3) the conviction is of an offence to be considered as an earlier offence` c

@ref s 286.1(4) (src:5804-5805)
GIVEN `the earlier convictions` IS A LIST OF `s 286.1(3) earlier conviction`
      `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.1(1) the person has committed a subsequent offence` MEANS
    IF any (GIVEN c IS A `s 286.1(3) earlier conviction` YIELD (`the conviction counts` c) EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the earlier convictions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF any (GIVEN c IS A `s 286.1(3) earlier conviction` YIELD (`the conviction counts` c) EQUALS NOTHING) `the earlier convictions`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): an earlier conviction of another offence, or on the same day, is not said to count or not to count
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for a first offence" (no earlier conviction under subsection (1) counts)
    WHERE
        `the conviction counts` c MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF (`s 286.1(4) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` (c's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`) `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the only question to be considered is the sequence of convictions"
                IF (`s 286.1(4) the conviction is earlier in the sequence of convictions` (c's `the day on which the person was convicted of that offence`) `the day on which the person was convicted of the offence for which sentence is being imposed`) EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): two convictions on one day
                IF c's `the offence of which the person was convicted`'s `section` EQUALS 286.1 AND c's `the offence of which the person was convicted`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" THEN JUST TRUE
                OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3)'s list is "for the purpose of subsection (2)"; the text does not say which earlier offences make an offence under subsection (1) a subsequent one

-- 286.1(2): the offence against a person under 18; indictable only; the minimum depends on first or subsequent.
-- src:5796 | Obtaining sexual services for consideration from person under 18 years
-- src:5797 | (2) Everyone who, in any place, obtains for consideration, or communicates with anyone for the purpose of obtaining for consideration, the sexual services of a person under the age of 18 years is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of
-- src:5798 | (a) for a first offence, six months; and
-- src:5799 | (b) for each subsequent offence, one year.
@ref s 286.1(2) (src:5796-5799)
GIVEN `s 197(1) the place is a place` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person obtains for consideration, or communicates with anyone for the purpose of obtaining for consideration, the sexual services of a person under the age of 18 years` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.1(2) the person is guilty of the offence of obtaining sexual services from a person under 18 years` MEANS
    IF `the person obtains for consideration, or communicates with anyone for the purpose of obtaining for consideration, the sexual services of a person under the age of 18 years` AND (`s 197(1) the place is a place` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who, in any place, obtains for consideration, or communicates with anyone for the purpose of obtaining for consideration, the sexual services of a person under the age of 18 years"

@ref s 286.1(2) (src:5796-5797)
`s 286.1(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 286.1(2) (src:5796-5799)
GIVEN `the answer of s 286.1(2) as to a subsequent offence` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Punishment
`s 286.1(2) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the answer of s 286.1(2) as to a subsequent offence`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), (`imprisonment for a term of` (`Length of time` OF 1, 0, 0, FALSE)), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST (Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), (`imprisonment for a term of` `six months`), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the offence is a subsequent one is not determined

§ `s 286.2 -- Material benefit from sexual services`

-- src:5809 | 286.2 (1) Every person who receives a financial or other material benefit, knowing that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 286.1(1), is guilty of
-- src:5810 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:5811 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 286.2(1) (src:5809-5811)
GIVEN `the person receives a financial or other material benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 286.1(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.2(1) the person is guilty of the offence of receiving a material benefit from sexual services` MEANS
    IF `the person receives a financial or other material benefit` AND `the person knows that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 286.1(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "knowing that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 286.1(1)"

@ref s 286.2(1) (src:5809-5811)
`s 286.2(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 286.2(1) (src:5810-5811)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 286.2(1) the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- src:5812 | Material benefit from sexual services provided by person under 18 years
-- src:5813 | (2) Everyone who receives a financial or other material benefit, knowing that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 286.1(2), is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of two years.
@ref s 286.2(2) (src:5812-5813)
GIVEN `the person receives a financial or other material benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 286.1(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.2(2) the person is guilty of the offence of receiving a material benefit from sexual services provided by a person under 18 years` MEANS
    IF `the person receives a financial or other material benefit` AND `the person knows that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 286.1(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "knowing that it is obtained by or derived directly or indirectly from the commission of an offence under subsection 286.1(2)"

@ref s 286.2(2) (src:5812-5813)
`s 286.2(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 286.2(2) (src:5812-5813)
`s 286.2(2) the punishment` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), (`imprisonment for a term of` `two years`), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- 286.2(3): the presumption "in the absence of evidence to the contrary" (fork F22: the same reading as s 279.01(3)).
-- src:5814 | Presumption
-- src:5815 | (3) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (2), evidence that a person lives with or is habitually in the company of a person who offers or provides sexual services for consideration is, in the absence of evidence to the contrary, proof that the person received a financial or other material benefit from those services.
@ref s 286.2(3) (src:5814-5815)
GIVEN `the person lives with or is habitually in the company of a person who offers or provides sexual services for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.2(3) the evidence is proof that the person received a financial or other material benefit from those services` MEANS
    IF `the person lives with or is habitually in the company of a person who offers or provides sexual services for consideration` AND (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the absence of evidence to the contrary"

-- 286.2(5) before (4): "Subsection (4) does not apply to a person who commits an offence under (1) or (2) if that person ...".
-- src:5822 | No exception
-- src:5823 | (5) Subsection (4) does not apply to a person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) if that person
-- src:5824 | (a) used, threatened to use or attempted to use violence, intimidation or coercion in relation to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived;
-- src:5825 | (b) abused a position of trust, power or authority in relation to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived;
-- src:5826 | (c) provided a drug, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived for the purpose of aiding or abetting that person to offer or provide sexual services for consideration;
-- src:5827 | (d) engaged in conduct, in relation to any person, that would constitute an offence under section 286.3; or
-- src:5828 | (e) received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise that offers sexual services for consideration.
@ref s 286.2(5) (src:5822-5828)
GIVEN `the person commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person used, threatened to use or attempted to use violence, intimidation or coercion in relation to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person abused a position of trust, power or authority in relation to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person provided a drug, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived for the purpose of aiding or abetting that person to offer or provide sexual services for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person engaged in conduct, in relation to any person, that would constitute an offence under section 286.3` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise that offers sexual services for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.2(5) subsection (4) does not apply to the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsection (4) does not apply to a person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) if that person"
        IF `the person used, threatened to use or attempted to use violence, intimidation or coercion in relation to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` OR `the person abused a position of trust, power or authority in relation to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` OR `the person provided a drug, alcohol or any other intoxicating substance to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived for the purpose of aiding or abetting that person to offer or provide sexual services for consideration` OR `the person engaged in conduct, in relation to any person, that would constitute an offence under section 286.3` OR `the person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise that offers sexual services for consideration` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if that person" (none of (a) to (e) holds: a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- 286.2(4): the exception, "Subject to subsection (5)", for a benefit received in one of four ways. Only the first answer of (5) matters here.
-- src:5816 | Exception
-- src:5817 | (4) Subject to subsection (5), subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person who receives the benefit
-- src:5818 | (a) in the context of a legitimate living arrangement with the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived;
-- src:5819 | (b) as a result of a legal or moral obligation of the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived;
-- src:5820 | (c) in consideration for a service or good that they offer, on the same terms and conditions, to the general public; or
-- src:5821 | (d) in consideration for a service or good that they do not offer to the general public but that they offered or provided to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived, if they did not counsel or encourage that person to provide sexual services and the benefit is proportionate to the value of the service or good.
@ref s 286.2(4) (src:5816-5821)
GIVEN `the person receives the benefit in the context of a legitimate living arrangement with the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receives the benefit as a result of a legal or moral obligation of the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receives the benefit in consideration for a service or good that they offer, on the same terms and conditions, to the general public` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person receives the benefit in consideration for a service or good that they do not offer to the general public but that they offered or provided to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they did not counsel or encourage that person to provide sexual services` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefit is proportionate to the value of the service or good` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 286.2(5)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.2(4) subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to the person who receives the benefit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 286.2(5)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (4) does not apply to a person who commits an offence under subsection (1) or (2) if that person" (subsection (5) takes the person out of the exception)
        IF `the person receives the benefit in the context of a legitimate living arrangement with the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` OR `the person receives the benefit as a result of a legal or moral obligation of the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` OR `the person receives the benefit in consideration for a service or good that they offer, on the same terms and conditions, to the general public` OR (`the person receives the benefit in consideration for a service or good that they do not offer to the general public but that they offered or provided to the person from whose sexual services the benefit is derived` AND `they did not counsel or encourage that person to provide sexual services` AND `the benefit is proportionate to the value of the service or good`) THEN (IF `the answer of s 286.2(5)` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE)   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (5) takes the person out of the exception is not determined
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to a person who receives the benefit" (none of (a) to (d) holds: a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:5829 | Aggravating factor
-- src:5830 | (6) If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court that imposes the sentence shall consider as an aggravating factor the fact that that person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise that offers sexual services for consideration.
@ref s 286.2(6) (src:5829-5830)
GIVEN `the person is convicted of an offence under section 286.2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise that offers sexual services for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.2(6) the court shall consider as an aggravating factor that the person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise` MEANS
    IF `the person is convicted of an offence under section 286.2` AND `the person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise that offers sexual services for consideration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person is convicted of an offence under this section, the court that imposes the sentence shall consider as an aggravating factor the fact that that person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise"

DECLARE `s 286.2(6) the act of the court` IS ONE OF `s 286.2(6) consider as an aggravating factor that the person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise that offers sexual services for consideration`

@ref s 286.2(6) (src:5829-5830)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 286.2(6) the act of the court`
`s 286.2(6) the duty of the court` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 286.2(6) consider as an aggravating factor that the person received the benefit in the context of a commercial enterprise that offers sexual services for consideration`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not consider the commercial enterprise as an aggravating factor"

§ `ss 286.3 and 286.4 -- Procuring and advertising`

-- src:5832 | 286.3 (1) Everyone who procures a person to offer or provide sexual services for consideration or, for the purpose of facilitating an offence under subsection 286.1(1), recruits, holds, conceals or harbours a person who offers or provides sexual services for consideration, or exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of that person, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years.
@ref s 286.3(1) (src:5832)
GIVEN `the person procures a person to offer or provide sexual services for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the purpose of facilitating an offence under subsection 286.1(1), the person recruits, holds, conceals or harbours a person who offers or provides sexual services for consideration, or exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.3(1) the person is guilty of the offence of procuring` MEANS
    IF `the person procures a person to offer or provide sexual services for consideration` OR `for the purpose of facilitating an offence under subsection 286.1(1), the person recruits, holds, conceals or harbours a person who offers or provides sexual services for consideration, or exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who procures a person to offer or provide sexual services for consideration or, for the purpose of facilitating an offence under subsection 286.1(1), recruits, holds, conceals or harbours a person"

@ref s 286.3(1) (src:5832)
`s 286.3(1) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 286.3(1) (src:5832)
`s 286.3(1) the punishment` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:5834 | (2) Everyone who procures a person under the age of 18 years to offer or provide sexual services for consideration or, for the purpose of facilitating an offence under subsection 286.1(2), recruits, holds, conceals or harbours a person under the age of 18 who offers or provides sexual services for consideration, or exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of that person, is guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 14 years and to a minimum punishment of imprisonment for a term of five years.
@ref s 286.3(2) (src:5834)
GIVEN `the person procures a person under the age of 18 years to offer or provide sexual services for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `for the purpose of facilitating an offence under subsection 286.1(2), the person recruits, holds, conceals or harbours a person under the age of 18 who offers or provides sexual services for consideration, or exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.3(2) the person is guilty of the offence of procuring a person under 18 years` MEANS
    IF `the person procures a person under the age of 18 years to offer or provide sexual services for consideration` OR `for the purpose of facilitating an offence under subsection 286.1(2), the person recruits, holds, conceals or harbours a person under the age of 18 who offers or provides sexual services for consideration, or exercises control, direction or influence over the movements of that person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who procures a person under the age of 18 years to offer or provide sexual services for consideration or, for the purpose of facilitating an offence under subsection 286.1(2)"

@ref s 286.3(2) (src:5834)
`s 286.3(2) the class of the offence` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref s 286.3(2) (src:5834)
`s 286.3(2) the punishment` MEANS Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`), (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

-- src:5836 | 286.4 Everyone who knowingly advertises an offer to provide sexual services for consideration is guilty of
-- src:5837 | (a) an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than five years; or
-- src:5838 | (b) an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 286.4 (src:5836-5838)
GIVEN `the person knowingly advertises an offer to provide sexual services for consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.4 the person is guilty of the offence of advertising sexual services` MEANS
    IF `the person knowingly advertises an offer to provide sexual services for consideration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone who knowingly advertises an offer to provide sexual services for consideration"

@ref s 286.4 (src:5836-5838)
`s 286.4 the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 286.4 (src:5837-5838)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 286.4 the punishment` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN Punishment OF `by indictment`, (`imprisonment for a term of` `five years`), `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

§ `s 286.5 -- Immunities`

-- 286.5(1): no prosecution for the benefit from one's own sexual services (286.2) or the advertisement of one's own (286.4). Not made out on an offence within the section: no immunity on these facts.
-- src:5840 | 286.5 (1) No person shall be prosecuted for
-- src:5841 | (a) an offence under section 286.2 if the benefit is derived from the provision of their own sexual services; or
-- src:5842 | (b) an offence under section 286.4 in relation to the advertisement of their own sexual services.
@ref s 286.5(1) (src:5840-5842)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the benefit is derived from the provision of their own sexual services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.5(1)(a) the person is immune from prosecution for an offence under section 286.2` MEANS
    IF NOT (offence's `section` EQUALS 286.2)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under section 286.2"
    ELSE IF `the benefit is derived from the provision of their own sexual services`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the benefit is derived from the provision of their own sexual services" (this section gives no immunity on these facts)

@ref s 286.5(1) (src:5840-5842)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the advertisement is of their own sexual services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.5(1)(b) the person is immune from prosecution for an offence under section 286.4` MEANS
    IF NOT (offence's `section` EQUALS 286.4)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence under section 286.4"
    ELSE IF `the advertisement is of their own sexual services`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in relation to the advertisement of their own sexual services" (this section gives no immunity on these facts)

-- The offence of s 286.2 after subsections (4) and (5) and the immunity of s 286.5(1)(a); the offence of s 286.4 after the immunity of s 286.5(1)(b).
@ref s 286.2 composed with s 286.5(1)(a) (src:5840-5842)
GIVEN `the answer of the offence function` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 286.2(4)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 286.5(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.2 and s 286.5(1)(a) the person is guilty of the offence after the exception and the immunity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the answer of s 286.2(4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of s 286.5(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsections (1) and (2) do not apply to a person who receives the benefit" or "No person shall be prosecuted for"
        IF (`the answer of the offence function` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 286.2(4)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the answer of s 286.5(1)(a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence, the exception or the immunity is not covered

@ref s 286.4 composed with s 286.5(1)(b) (src:5840-5842)
GIVEN `the answer of the offence function` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of s 286.5(1)(b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.4 and s 286.5(1)(b) the person is guilty of the offence after the immunity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the answer of s 286.5(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No person shall be prosecuted for"
        IF (`the answer of the offence function` EQUALS JUST TRUE) AND (`the answer of s 286.5(1)(b)` EQUALS JUST FALSE) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the offence or the immunity is not covered

-- src:5844 | (2) No person shall be prosecuted for aiding, abetting, conspiring or attempting to commit an offence under any of sections 286.1 to 286.4 or being an accessory after the fact or counselling a person to be a party to such an offence, if the offence relates to the offering or provision of their own sexual services.
@ref s 286.5(2) (src:5844)
GIVEN offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the person is accused of aiding, abetting, conspiring or attempting to commit the offence, of being an accessory after the fact, or of counselling a person to be a party to it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence relates to the offering or provision of their own sexual services` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 286.5(2) the person is immune from prosecution for being a party to an offence under any of sections 286.1 to 286.4` MEANS
    IF NOT (offence's `section` AT LEAST 286.1 AND offence's `section` AT MOST 286.4 AND `the person is accused of aiding, abetting, conspiring or attempting to commit the offence, of being an accessory after the fact, or of counselling a person to be a party to it`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "aiding, abetting, conspiring or attempting to commit an offence under any of sections 286.1 to 286.4 or being an accessory after the fact or counselling a person to be a party to such an offence"
    ELSE IF `the offence relates to the offering or provision of their own sexual services`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the offence relates to the offering or provision of their own sexual services" (this section gives no immunity on these facts)
